      <place id="p24"><name><text>p24</text></name></place>
      <place id="p25"><name><text>end</text></name></place>
      <place id="p26"><name><text>p26</text></name></place>
      <transition id="t01"><name><text>1. President to House plenary: President's budget: NEP, BESF, Budget Message, within 30 days from the opening of the regular session</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t02"><name><text>2. House plenary to House Appropriations: The NEP is filed as the General Appropriations Bill (GAB) and referred to the committee</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t03"><name><text>3. DBCC to House Appropriations: Briefing on the economy and the fiscal program</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau1"><name><text>parallel split</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau2"><name><text>parallel join</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t04"><name><text>4. House Appropriations to National agency: Hearings, agency by agency: plans, past performance</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t05"><name><text>5. National agency to House Appropriations: Answers and documents</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t06"><name><text>6. Senate Finance to National agency: Hearings, agency by agency</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t07"><name><text>7. National agency to Senate Finance: Answers and documents</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t08"><name><text>8. House Appropriations to House plenary: Committee report on the GAB</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t09"><name><text>9. House plenary: Plenary debates and amendments. Approval on second and third reading</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t10"><name><text>10. House plenary to Senate plenary: GAB as approved by the House</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t11"><name><text>11. Senate Finance to Senate plenary: Committee report with Senate amendments</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t12"><name><text>12. Senate plenary: Plenary debates and amendments. Approval on second and third reading</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t13"><name><text>13. House plenary to Bicameral committee: House conferees and House version</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t14"><name><text>14. Senate plenary to Bicameral committee: Senate conferees and Senate version</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t15"><name><text>15. Bicameral committee: Reconcile the two versions</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t16"><name><text>16. Bicameral committee to House plenary: Conference report</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t17"><name><text>17. Bicameral committee to Senate plenary: Conference report</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t18"><name><text>18. House plenary to President: Both chambers ratify. The enrolled bill goes to the President</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t19"><name><text>19. President: Review. May veto particular items. The items not vetoed become law</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t20"><name><text>20. President to DBM: Signed General Appropriations Act (GAA)</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau3"><name><text>skip: Congress disagrees with a veto</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="t21"><name><text>21. House plenary to President: Override by two thirds of each chamber</text></name></transition>
      <transition id="tau4"><name><text>end of: Congress disagrees with a veto</text></name></transition>
